# What NOT to send to the builder.
#
# Docker does not read .gitignore, and without this file the build context is
# the whole folder: .venv is 307 MB and hkrd.db is 31 MB, neither of which the
# image wants. Both would be uploaded to Fly's remote builder on every deploy,
# and the database would sit in the context of an image whose whole design is
# that the database lives on a volume instead.
#
# A denylist rather than an allowlist. The Dockerfile COPYs five things —
# pyproject.toml, README.md, hkrd/, web/, ops/ — and an allowlist would make a
# sixth silently arrive empty. Anything added here fails loudly instead.

# The virtualenv. The image builds its own from pyproject.toml.
.venv/
venv/

# The database. It belongs on the Fly volume, put there once by
# `fly sftp put` — see ops/install-db.sh and docs/deploy.md.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# History. The image is built from a checkout; it does not need the checkout's
# past, and .git grows without bound.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Build and test leavings.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Not in the image: the Dockerfile copies neither, and docs/ changing should
# not invalidate a layer.
tests/
docs/

# Secrets. These are Fly secrets in the deployed environment and must never be
# baked into a layer, where `docker history` would read them back.
.env
.env.*

# Scraped artefacts — these go in tables, not files (AGENTS.md, Data rules).
reports/
cache/
racecards/

# Local editor state.
*.code-workspace
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
